            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Administration and Policies</strong><br>\nAdams' administration focused on strengthening the federal government and developing international respect for the new nation. He oversaw the creation of the Navy Department and the Marine Corps, which played significant roles in protecting American interests abroad.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Later Years and Legacy</strong><br>\nAfter losing the presidential election of 1800 to Thomas Jefferson, Adams retired to Massachusetts. He spent the remaining years of his life writing and reflecting on his political career. Adams' legacy as a founding father and leader has remained influential in American history.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Death and Historical Impact</strong><br>\nJohn Adams died on July 4, 1826, on the 50th anniversary of the Declaration of Independence. His passing marked the end of an era for the original American patriots. Adams is remembered as a steadfast leader whose work helped lay the foundations of the United States government.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
